{
  "version": 291,
  "released": "2026-09-04",
  "changelog": "v291: Add Landmark reads what you paste ONCE, with everything it needs in front of it. Owner rulings R6-R9 of 2026-09-04, an amendment to ADR 0033. Until now the offer path read a submission three times — a deterministic block grammar first, then the general listener over the whole document blind to what the grammar had taken, then one focused recorder per domain, also blind. Pasting a thirty-stay residence history into it produced eight stays labelled by their city, a second dateless residence made out of a street name, every school and job dateless, invented labels, bracketed dates read as certain, whole blocks dumped into stories because they carried a parenthetical, and \"inferred\" printed over units where nothing had been read at all. The cause was the ORDER, not the model: a deterministic reader ran in front of the interaction and hid its own work from it. R6 reverses it — **the interaction reads; the system validates and files.** New `interactions/landmarks/prompt/reading.md` is the one leaf, and it carries, RENDERED FROM THE LIVE TABLES rather than hand-copied, the nine domains and the exact keys each can read, the E-L2c name fields probed one at a time out of `validate_landmark` itself, which domains take a stretch and which take one date, the accepted date forms, the estimation conventions, the relation rule, the roster and what is already filed — plus two whole worked readings, one document block and one sentence of prose. New `system/landmark_reading.py` parses the completion: lenient in shape (a missing list is empty, an unknown key is dropped with a finding, a completion that is not JSON at all is an empty reading with a finding and never an exception) and strict in substance (every quote must LOCATE in the submitted text, dangling and cyclic `within` refs are findings and the unit survives with no parent, every record goes through `landmarks_interaction.validate_landmark`). **What you will notice.** A school or a job named inside a stay now belongs to that stay (R7) and takes its dates, marked as an inference and carrying the sentence that earned it — \"from the dates of the Avenue F stay\" — instead of showing up dateless. A bracketed or hedged bound reads as YOUR estimate and says \"estimated, as you marked it\" (R8) instead of being flattened to certain. A unit nothing dated says \"no date read\" and asks the domain's own question, instead of claiming an inference nobody made. A bound your text does not carry is DROPPED with a finding rather than rewritten into a confident-looking guess. Nicknames, cities, addresses and links now ride on the unit as its NAMES, which is how a story told next year about \"the blue house\" finds its way back to the stay. Events are read and carried as their own list (dated ones marked for filing as claims, undated ones as moments held inside their stay); Cut 6g files them. **Hosts must thread four new things**: `within` and `names` on every unit, the new `events` list on the proposal, and the `reading` completion key — `host_listener_prompt` is now `host_reading_prompt` returning `{\"reading\": {prompt, model, prompt_version}}`, `host_recorder_prompts` and the `--listener-completion` flag are DELETED with the pass they named, and `--completions` now takes `{\"reading\": <completion>}`. A unit's `dates` block gained `estimated` `{start, end}`, `inherited_from` and `clause`, and its `basis` is now one of stated | inferred | none. Also fixed at the shared root: `landmark_offer.date_evidence` accepted a month only by its full name, so a date written the way v290's own reader parses it (`Jun 1986`) was dropped as unevidenced — it now reads the 3-letter abbreviation too, from `chronology.MONTH_NAMES` rather than a fourth private copy; and `locate` honours its `hint` on the whitespace-tolerant path, so a document that repeats itself (the same employer on three consecutive blocks) locates three quotes instead of three copies of the first. Collect mode — the daily listener and the focused recorder — is untouched. `grammar_units` survives this release uncalled; Cut 6h deletes it. New: `system/landmark_reading.py`, `interactions/landmarks/prompt/reading.md`, `tests/test_landmark_reading.py`; the five offer goldens are replaced.",
